## 3. Keyboard Ergonomics & Keystroke Budget

The keyboard interface is optimized so common actions take **1 or 2 keys**:

| User Intent | Keystroke | Behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Command help** (unified) | **`Tab`** / **`Shift+Tab`** (empty draft) | Opens `/help · Commands & AI` or steps back to the prior view when already on help. Pushes `viewHistory`. |
| **Interaction history** | **`←`** / **`→`** (empty draft) | Navigates `viewHistory` (max 12). Slash entries re-run on draw; AI entries are frozen snapshots. |
| **Toggle debug page** | **`Ctrl+D`** | Flips `interactionPage` `main` ↔ `debug` when the active widget has `debugPage`. Does not insert a character into the draft. Exit remains **`Esc`** / **`Ctrl+C`** only. |
| **Autocomplete Slash Command** | **`Tab`** or **`Right Arrow`** (when draft starts with `/`) | If the user typed a prefix like `/p` or `/b`, completes it to the matching command (`/peers`, `/buckets`). Even better: submitting an unambiguous prefix like `/p` + `Enter` resolves directly! |
| **Run Command or AI Query** | Type text + **`Enter`** | Routes `promptDraft` through `IntentEngine` and mounts the resulting `WidgetSpec` in the Main Interaction Area. |
| **History Navigation** | **`Up` / `Down`** | Cycles through submitted prompt history. |
| **Exit Cleanly** | **`Esc`** or **`Ctrl+C`** | Restores terminal screen and exits. |

---

## 4. Separation & Testing Invariants

- `renderFrame` and widget/box renderers must stay 100% free of `node:*`, `process.stdout`, `stdin`, and spine mutation.
- Virtual framebuffer tests (`test/tui.spec.ts`) must verify:
  - `lines.length === rows` and every line `visibleWidth(line) === cols`.
  - `Tab` help toggle and `viewHistory` navigation keep column coordinates stable.
  - `Ctrl+D` toggles debug sections for widgets with `debugPage` without changing `cols`/`rows` line count.
  - Pressing `Enter` on an empty draft triggers the active domain's deep view in the Main Interaction Area, whereas pressing `Tab` alone preserves any existing `activeWidget` in the Main Area.
